# errors.json content rules that tests enforce: the {{description}} of each grouped code (9001, 9002, 9003, 9004, 9005, 9050, 9051) starts with {{"Grouped code"}} (e.g. 9001: "Grouped code - no longer raised since firmware 1.0.106: replaced by 9010 (chamber), 9011 (left), 9012 (right), one code per component. Kept so older reports and logs still show a title. ..."); every per-component member has the same severity as its family, a non-empty {{troubleshooting}} list and a {{videoUrl}} field present (empty string until service fills it). 9052 has non-empty troubleshooting. Descriptions/troubleshooting are operator prose (the source file is ~80 KB); OPEN QUESTION: the full prose is not reproduced here — if the original {{config/errors.json}} is available copy it verbatim, otherwise write a description and 2-4 troubleshooting lines per record that state the trigger, thresholds and effect documented in the relevant DOM ticket (e.g. 9010: open for >= 60 s, immediate while heating, no process can start, clears when the sensor reads; 9017: heartbeat silent 20 s, re-cut every 5 s, latched until acknowledged).
