*Behaviour & rules:*
# NTC (Murata NCP21XV103J03RA, 10 kOhm, β 3934, topology 3.3 V -> 10 kOhm -> tap (ADC) -> NTC -> GND): {{VoltageToResistance(v)}} = null if {{v <= 0 || v >= 3.3}}, else {{10000 * v / (3.3 - v)}}. {{ResistanceToTemperature(R)}} = null if null or {{<= 0}}, else {{1 / (1/298.15 + ln(R/10000)/3934) - 273.15}}. Higher tap volts = colder. Valid supervised range -20..120 °C.
# Chamber calibration (TC-08 reference, 2026-08-04, 724 paired samples): {{Static(raw) = 1.0979*raw - 3.9813}}. {{Correct(raw, seconds)}}: enqueue (seconds, raw); drop samples with {{seconds - t > 45}}; est = Static(raw); if fewer than 3 samples or span (last.t - first.t) < 10 s -> est. Rate = least-squares slope of raw vs t (centred on mean t) * 60 (°C/min); den <= 0 -> est. If {{rate > 0.3}}: est += {{2.1873 * (rate - 0.3)}}. Else if {{rate < -1.0}}: {{f = min(1, (-1.0 - rate) / (-1.0 - -2.5))}}, est += {{f * 0.0956 * (raw - 25)}}. Rates between -1.0 and 0.3 add nothing. {{Correct(raw)}} uses the TimeProvider (seconds elapsed since construction via {{GetTimestamp}}/{{GetElapsedTime}}); without a TimeProvider it throws {{InvalidOperationException("no TimeProvider: use Correct(rawC, seconds)")}}. {{Reset()}} clears the window. One instance per sensor; not thread-safe.
# Pressure (SMC ISE20 analog output on ADS1115 U7 AIN3): {{saturated = vAdc >= AdcSaturationVolts}}; {{vSensor = vAdc * Divider}}. analog_voltage and not saturated: {{mpa = PAtLow + (vSensor - VMin) * (PAtHigh - PAtLow) / (VMax - VMin)}} (1 V = 0 MPa, 5 V = 1.000 MPa, 0.6 V = -0.100 MPa). analog_current and not saturated: {{iMa = vSensor / ShuntOhms * 1000}}, {{mpa = PAtLow + (iMa - IMinMa) * (PAtHigh - PAtLow) / (IMaxMa - IMinMa)}}. {{On}}: switch mode -> {{vAdc >= OnAboveVolts}}; else mpa known -> {{mpa >= SetPointMpa}} (0.1 MPa = 1 bar); else {{On = saturated}} (clamped analog = pressure above span). {{Bar = mpa * 10}}; Mpa/Bar null when saturated or in switch mode. Result carries Volts = vAdc, SensorVolts, Mode, SetPointMpa.
# {{SlopeEstimator.Add(t, v)}}: append, then drop from the front while {{t - first.t > WindowSec}}. {{SlopePerSecond(samples, minSpan)}}: null if count < 3 or {{last.t - first.t < minSpan}}; least squares with x = t - t0 centred on its mean; den <= 0 -> null. {{RatePerMinute = slope * 60}}.
# {{TachRateTracker}} (owner locks; all readers share one sample history per key so interleaved readers get the same rate): constructor throws {{ArgumentOutOfRangeException}} for {{pulsesPerRev <= 0}} (hardware uses 2). {{Rpm(key, count, now)}}: if {{count < last stored count}} clear the samples (counter restarted). Append {{(count, now)}} if the list is empty or {{now - newest.At >= 0.1 - 1e-6}}. While there are >= 2 samples and {{now - samples[1].At >= 1.0 - 1e-6}}, remove samples[0] (keep as reference the newest sample at least one window old). {{window = now - samples[0].At}}; if {{window < 1.0 - 1e-6}} return the last rate for the key (null if none). Else {{rpm = (int)Math.Round((count - ref.Count) / pulsesPerRev * (60 / window))}}, store and return. (Fixes a false Err 9002 where a second reader 4 ms later saw 0 RPM.)
# {{SensorGlitchHold}} (owner locks): {{Good(key, value, now)}}: store last good (value, now), clear the expired flag; if a bad episode was open, remove it and return its duration ({{now - badSince}}), else null. {{Bad(key, now, holdSec, out held)}}: {{first = badSince.TryAdd(key, now)}}; if {{holdSec <= 0}} or no good value yet -> {{Report}}; if {{(now - lastGood.At).TotalSeconds <= holdSec}} -> held = last good value, {{HoldStarted}} if first else {{Holding}}; otherwise {{HoldExpired}} the first time (expired flag added), {{Report}} afterwards. The window counts from the last GOOD reading, not from the first bad one.
*Configuration:* {{PressureSensorParameters}} is filled by the Hardware layer from components.json {{pressure_sensor}}: {{mode}} "analog_voltage", {{v_min}} 1.0, {{v_max}} 5.0, {{i_min_ma}} 4.0, {{i_max_ma}} 20.0, {{shunt_ohms}} 120.0, {{p_at_v_min_mpa}} 0.0, {{p_at_v_max_mpa}} 1.0, {{divider}} 1.0, {{adc_saturation_volts}} 3.2, {{on_above_volts}} 2.0, {{set_point_mpa}} 0.1. The glitch hold seconds come from components.json {{sensor_filter.glitch_hold_sec}} (15; 0 disables). TachRateTracker pulses per rev = 2 (Hardware {{IoBoardMap.PulsesPerRev}}).
*Acceptance criteria:*
* NTC: 1.65 V -> 10000 Ohm and 25.0 °C; 10000 Ohm -> 25 °C; 0.0, -0.1, 3.3, 3.5 V -> null; the β-equation 50 °C resistance and its tap voltage both give 50.0 °C; 2.5 V < 25 °C; R null or 0 -> null.
* Calibration: static only for (50,0),(51,5),(52,9); steady 60 °C gives Static(60); raw +1.0 °C/min over 45 s (0.25 °C each 15 s) -> Static(50.75) + 2.1873*0.7; +0.2 °C/min -> static; -3 °C/min -> + 0.0956*(57.75-25); -1.75 °C/min -> + 0.5*0.0956*(58.6875-25); -0.5 °C/min -> static; samples older than 45 s dropped; TimeProvider constructor stamps samples (FakeTimeProvider advancing 15 s).
* Pressure (saturation lifted to 5.5 V): 0.6 V -> -0.100 MPa, 1.0 -> 0, 3.4 -> 0.600, 5.0 -> 1.000, Bar = 10x, Mode "analog_voltage"; Default 1.0 V -> On false; 1.39 V off, 1.41 V on, SetPointMpa 0.1; Default 3.2 / 3.3 V -> Mpa/Bar null, Saturated, On, Volts echoed; divider 2.0 at 1.7 V -> SensorVolts 3.4, 0.6 MPa; current mode 0.288 / 0.48 / 2.4 V -> -0.1 / 0 / 1.0 MPa; switch mode 0.52 V off with null Mpa, 2.0 and 3.3 V on, Mode "switch".
* Slope: null with (0,20),(5,21); null at 9 s span; non-null once (10,23) added; linear -0.1/s -> -6.0 per minute; window 10 keeps 11 samples t=30..40, rate 60; all-equal t -> null.
* Tach (150 edges/s, 2 ppr): null at 0 and 0.5 s, 4500 at 1.0 s; two readers 4 ms apart stay within 4400..4600 for 40 s; stopped fan -> 0 at 6.6 s; independent keys 3000/1500; counter restart returns the last rate (1500) until a new window, then 3000; a reader every 1 ms for 10 s stays within 4400..4600.
* Glitch: Bad without Good -> Report; Good 42.5 at T0 then Bad at +1 HoldStarted (42.5), +30 Holding (42.5), +30.5 HoldExpired, +60 Report; Good at +20 after Bad at +10 returns 10 s, then Bad at +45 HoldStarted (21.0), +51 HoldExpired; keys independent; holdSec 0 -> Report.
