*Behaviour & rules — fans:*
# {{CriticalFor(fan)}} = per-fan override if present, else {{CriticalBelowPct}}.
# {{ExpectedRpm(points, duty)}}: null if null/empty; sort by duty; {{duty <= first.duty}} -> {{first.rpm * duty / first.duty}} (proportional); between two points -> linear interpolation; above the last -> {{last.rpm * duty / last.duty}}.
# {{Evaluate(rules, fan, duty, rpm, now)}} (call once per fan per tick, then {{Finish}}): if no duty seen or {{|seenDuty - duty| > 0.5}} -> remember (duty, now) (settle clock). {{expected = duty > 0 ? ExpectedRpm(Nominal[fan], duty) : null}}. Base entry {{(duty, rpm, expected > 0 ? (int)expected : null, null, "idle", null)}}. Judged only if {{duty >= MinEvalDuty && expected > 0 && rpm != null && now - dutySeenAt >= SettleSec}}; otherwise forget below-since and record "idle". {{deficit = Math.Round((1 - rpm/expected) * 100, 1)}}; {{persist = rpm <= 0.05*expected ? StoppedPersistSec : PersistSec}}; {{level = deficit >= CriticalFor(fan) ? "critical" : deficit >= WarnBelowPct ? "warn" : "ok"}}. ok -> forget below-since, record {{(DeficitPct = deficit, Status "ok")}}. Else below-since = existing (level0, since) or (level, now); if level0 was critical and level is warn -> since = now (a shallower deficit restarts the clock); store (level, since); {{below = now - since}}; status = below >= persist ? level : level + "-pending"; entry with DeficitPct, {{Since = (int)below}}. When {{below >= persist}}: detail = {{$"{HardwareNames.Label(fan)}: {rpm} RPM measured, {(int)expected} RPM expected at {duty:0} % duty ({deficit:0} % below nominal for {(int)below} s)"}}; overridden fan -> Status "overridden" (no action); critical -> critical detail stored, add to the critical latch set and, if new, to NewlyCritical; warn -> warn detail stored.
# Record: store Health[fan]; if Status != "warn" drop the fan's warn detail; Rebuild: drop critical details of fans no longer latched; for family 9002 remove 9002 and all members then add {{FanFailureOf(fan) -> detail}} for every critical detail; same for 9051 with {{FanWearOf}} and warn details.
# {{Finish(rules, now)}}: for each latched critical fan: if its Health status is "ok", start/keep ok-since and release the latch once {{now - okSince >= PersistSec}}; else forget ok-since. Rebuild; return {{(copy of Alerts, NewlyCritical since last Finish)}} and clear NewlyCritical. A latched fan that goes idle (because 9002 stopped every output) stays latched.
# {{BlockingCritical}} = latched fans not overridden, ordered by name (ordinal) — they block every process start. {{SetOverride(fans, on)}}: on -> add to override set and remove from the latch; off -> remove override; Rebuild; on also clears all 9030-9034 alerts. Overridden fans are still reported (status "overridden") but never latch, alert or block.
# {{Acknowledge()}} (operator deletes the alarm): release the latch of every latched fan whose Health status is not "critical" (idle or ok), also forgetting ok-since and below-since, adding {{"{FanFailureOf(fan)} {fan}"}} (e.g. {{"9022 FAN_LEFT"}}) to the result; remove all 9030-9034 alerts and if any was removed add {{"903x"}}; Rebuild; return the list. A fan driven and failing right now keeps its latch.
# {{SetFanStopped(tested, stopped)}}: remove grouped 9003; for each tested fan: {{alerts[FanStoppedOf(fan)] = detail}} if in {{stopped}}, else remove that code. Untested fans keep their state (LED-fan and cooling-fan pre-flights run at different starts). (FAN_HEATER in {{tested}} throws.)
*Behaviour & rules — LED panels (9040-9045 not heating, 9042/9043 drop):*
# {{Label}}: {{"Left LED"}}, {{"Right LED"}}, {{"Back LED"}}, default {{"Door LED"}}.
# Per panel in {{rules.Panels}} (panel -> its thermistor), with a per-panel window {Base, LitSec, LitAt?, LastLit, Verdict?, FailAt, Peak?, PeakChamber?, IntSeen?, SettleUntil, DropSince?}: base entry {{(isLit, isLit ? intensity : 0, null, null, 0, "off", null, null)}}.
# Lit and {{intensity >= MinEvalIntensity}}: {{t = readTemp(sensor)}}; not {{ReadOk}} -> status "no-sensor", window untouched, next panel. Window: if none, or (not lit last tick and {{now - LastLit > RestSec}}) -> new window {Base = temp, LitSec 0, LitAt now, LastLit now, FailAt = CheckAfterSec, SettleUntil = MinValue}; else if not lit last tick (re-lit within RestSec) -> keep Base and LitSec, LitAt = now, FailAt = LitSec + CheckAfterSec, Verdict/Peak/DropSince/IntSeen = null, SettleUntil = now; else LitSec += now - LitAt, LitAt = now. LastLit = now. {{rise = temp - Base}}; entry Baseline = round(Base,1), Rise = round(rise,2), LitSec = (int)LitSec. {{dropped}} = panel currently in the drop latch. If Verdict "ok" or rise >= MinRiseC -> status "ok", Verdict "ok", and if latched not-heating and rise >= MinRiseC release it. Else if LitSec >= FailAt and not dropped -> status "fail", Verdict "fail", latch not-heating with {{$"{label}: +{rise:0.0} C after {(int)LitSec} s at {intensity:0} % (at least {MinRiseC:0.0} C expected) - check that the {label} connector is plugged in"}}. Else "warming".
# Drop tracking when Verdict "ok": first time IntSeen = intensity; a change {{> 0.5}} -> IntSeen = intensity, Peak = null, DropSince = null, SettleUntil = now + DropSettleSec. When {{now >= SettleUntil}}: if Peak null or temp > Peak -> Peak = temp, PeakChamber = chamber; {{comp = max(0, PeakChamber - chamber)}} when both known else 0; {{drop = (Peak - temp) - comp}}; entry Peak = round(Peak,1), Drop = round(drop,2). {{drop >= DropC}} -> DropSince ??= now; lasted >= DropPersistSec -> latch drop with {{$"{label}: fell {drop:0.0} C below its {Peak:0.0} C peak while lit at {intensity:0} % (chamber cooling taken off) for {(int)lasted} s - the panel stopped heating mid-process, check the {label} connector and driver output"}}. Else DropSince = null and, if it was dropped and {{drop <= DropC/2}}, release the drop latch. If drop-latched -> status "drop".
# Not lit, or lit below MinEvalIntensity: if the window was lit (LitAt set) -> LastLit = LitAt, LitAt = null (only light seen between lit ticks counts). Status "low" if lit (too dim); then "fail" if not-heating latched; then "drop" if drop latched. Latches survive the panel going off.
# Alerts: remove 9004 and its members, then add {{LedNotHeatingOf(panel) -> detail}} for latched panels in order LEFT, RIGHT, BACK, DOOR; same for 9005 with {{LedTempDropOf}} (throws for BACK/DOOR — only Left/Right are ever configured).
*Behaviour & rules — UV light (9046 / 9047, warning only, thresholds not yet calibrated on a unit):*
# {{IsLit(volts, baseline, ratio)}} = null without baseline, else {{volts <= baseline * ratio}}.
# {{Evaluate}}: disabled -> clear baselines, lit-since and alerts, return. For UV_LEFT then UV_RIGHT (panel = {{sensor.Panel()}}, code = {{UvLightNotDetectedOf(panel)}}, {{v = readVolts(sensor)}}, {{usable = 0 < v < 3.3}}): panel not lit -> forget lit-since, remove the alert, and if usable store v as dark baseline. Lit but {{intensity < MinIntensity}} -> forget lit-since, remove alert. Otherwise start lit-since if new; if v null or no baseline -> no judgement; if {{IsLit == true}} -> remove alert; else if {{now - litSince >= ConfirmSec}} and no alert yet -> {{alerts[code] = Describe(sensor, litSec, v, dark)}}. Back/Door panels have no photoresistor and are never judged. Nothing is stopped.
# {{Describe}} = {{$"{Left|Right} UV panel lit for {(int)litSec} s but its UV sensor ({sensor}) still reads dark: {volts:0.00} V (dark {dark:0.00} V)"}}.
