public sealed record PressureReading(double Volts, double? Mpa, double? Bar, bool On, bool Saturated, string Mode, double SetPointMpa);
public sealed class HardwareRefusedException : Exception { public HardwareRefusedException(string message); }
public sealed class HardwareVerifyException : Exception { public HardwareVerifyException(string message); public HardwareVerifyException(string message, Exception inner); }
```
*Behaviour & rules:*
# All members must be thread-safe; compound register sequences are serialised on one lock inside the implementation.
# Refusals (door not confirmed closed, LED not allowed in the wavelength, routing read-back mismatch, LED_SWITCH not confirmed, DVT hang drop) throw {{HardwareRefusedException}}. Read-back mismatch after retries or I2C/bus errors throw {{HardwareVerifyException}}.
# {{DoorOpen()}} null must never be treated as "open" or as "closed" by callers; LEDs require it to be exactly {{false}}.
# {{ReadRpm}} is non-blocking and returns the same value to every reader (shared window >= 1 s); null until a first window exists. {{MeasureRpm}} blocks for {{window}}.
# {{SetLed}} takes a *physical* brightness percent; it enforces min intensity, door closed, wavelength gating and the SSR turn-on order, and starts/stops the panel's fan.
# The hardware layer itself raises no numeric error codes; the Api/Application layers map {{HardwareRefusedException}} to code 6015 ({{ErrorCodes.HardwareRefused}}).
*Configuration:* none (exposes {{Config}}).
*Acceptance criteria:*
* The interface compiles with exactly the members above (names and signatures exact).
* {{PressureReading}} is a positional record with the 7 fields in the order given.
*Tests:* covered through {{IoBoardHardwareSystemTests}} and {{SimulatedHardwareSystemTests}} (HW-11, HW-12, HW-15).
*Reference (source):* {{src/SCureBox.Hardware/IHardwareSystem.cs}}, {{src/SCureBox.Hardware/SCureBox.Hardware.csproj}}

