*Goal:* Provide plain GPIO outputs/inputs over libgpiod (never pinctrl, except the watchdog) and free-running rising-edge counters for the six fan tachometers. The tach lines are requested directly through libgpiod v2 in ONE request (input + pull-up + rising edge) because System.Device.Gpio's open-then-reconfigure fails with EINVAL on the CM5.
*Depends on:* none in area (System.Device.Gpio 4.2.0)
*Files to create:*
* {{src/SCureBox.Hardware/Bus/IGpioPins.cs}} - {{internal interface IGpioPins : IDisposable}}
* {{src/SCureBox.Hardware/Bus/SystemDeviceGpioPins.cs}} - {{internal sealed class SystemDeviceGpioPins : IGpioPins}}
* {{src/SCureBox.Hardware/Bus/LibgpiodDrivers.cs}} - {{internal static class LibgpiodDrivers}}
* {{src/SCureBox.Hardware/Bus/LibgpiodEdgeCounter.cs}} - {{internal sealed class LibgpiodEdgeCounter : IDisposable}}
* Test fake: {{tests/SCureBox.Hardware.Tests/Fakes/FakeGpioPins.cs}}
*Public contract:*
```csharp
internal interface IGpioPins : IDisposable {
    void OpenOutput(int pin, bool initialHigh);   // idempotent
    void OpenInput(int pin, bool pullUp);         // idempotent; pullUp false = no pull
    void Write(int pin, bool high);               // throws InvalidOperationException if not an open output
    bool Read(int pin);                           // inputs and outputs (read-back); throws when unreadable
    void OpenCounter(int pin);                    // pull-up input counting rising edges; idempotent
    long ReadCounter(int pin);                    // throws InvalidOperationException if not a counter
}
internal sealed class SystemDeviceGpioPins : IGpioPins { public SystemDeviceGpioPins(int gpioChip); public static int DetectRp1Chip(); }
internal static class LibgpiodDrivers { public static GpioDriver Create(int gpioChip); }
internal sealed class LibgpiodEdgeCounter : IDisposable {
    internal const int DirectionInput = 2; internal const int BiasPullUp = 4; internal const int EdgeRising = 2;
    public LibgpiodEdgeCounter(int gpioChip, int pin, string consumer);
    public int Pin { get; } public long Count { get; } public string? ReaderFault { get; }
}
```
*Behaviour & rules:*
# {{LibgpiodDrivers.Create(chip)}}: try {{new LibGpiodV2Driver(chip)}}; on {{PlatformNotSupportedException}}/{{DllNotFoundException}}/{{EntryPointNotFoundException}}/{{TypeInitializationException}} try {{new LibGpiodDriver(chip)}} (v1); if that fails the same way throw {{PlatformNotSupportedException("libgpiod not usable: v2 - {m2}; v1 - {m1}")}}. (Debian Trixie ships only libgpiod v2.)
# {{SystemDeviceGpioPins(chip)}} wraps {{new GpioController(LibgpiodDrivers.Create(chip))}}; all ops under one private lock; tracks sets of outputs and inputs.
# {{OpenOutput}}: return if already an output; open pin if not open; {{SetPinMode(Output)}}; write initial level; move pin from inputs to outputs. {{OpenInput}}: return if already an input; open; mode {{InputPullUp}} or {{Input}}; move to inputs. {{Write}} requires an open output. {{Read}} requires the pin to be open (else {{InvalidOperationException("GPIO{pin} is not open")}}), returns {{== High}}.
# {{OpenCounter}}: idempotent; throws {{InvalidOperationException("GPIO{pin} is already open through the GPIO controller")}} if the controller holds the pin; else creates {{LibgpiodEdgeCounter(chip, pin, "scurebox-tach")}}. {{ReadCounter}} returns {{Count}}.
# {{DetectRp1Chip()}}: if {{/sys/class/gpio}} missing -> 0; else for each {{gpiochip*}} dir whose {{label}} file trims to {{pinctrl-rp1}}, resolve the {{device}} link; if its name is {{gpiochipN}} return N. Any exception -> 0. Default 0.
# {{LibgpiodEdgeCounter}} P/Invokes {{libgpiod.so.3}}: {{gpiod_chip_open("/dev/gpiochip{chip}")}}, {{gpiod_line_settings_new/set_direction(2)/set_bias(4)/set_edge_detection(2)}}, {{gpiod_line_config_new/add_line_settings(offsets=[pin], 1)}}, {{gpiod_request_config_new/set_consumer}}, {{gpiod_chip_request_lines}}, {{gpiod_edge_event_buffer_new(64)}}; settings/configs freed in finally; on failure release request + close chip and throw {{InvalidOperationException("GPIO{pin} tachometer: {what} (errno N)")}}. A background thread ({{IsBackground}}, name {{tach-GPIO{pin}}}) loops: {{wait_edge_events(timeout 100 ms)}}; 0 -> continue; <0 -> set {{ReaderFault}}, sleep 100 ms; then {{read_edge_events(buffer, 64)}} and {{Interlocked.Add(count, read)}} (every event is a rising edge). Dispose: stop flag, join 1 s, free buffer, release request, close chip (idempotent).
# {{FakeGpioPins}} (test): levels dict, counters dict, {{Journal}} lines {{"gpio{pin} <- 0|1"}} on Write, {{Outputs}}, {{Inputs}}, {{PullUps}}, {{Unreadable}} (Read throws IOException), {{SetInput}}, {{AddPulses}}, {{Level}}. {{OpenCounter}} = {{OpenInput(pin, true)}} + counter 0.
*Configuration:* {{HardwareOptions.GpioChip}} (null = {{DetectRp1Chip()}}).
*Acceptance criteria:*
* {{LibgpiodEdgeCounter.DirectionInput == 2}}, {{BiasPullUp == 4}}, {{EdgeRising == 2}}.
* Writing a pin that is not an open output throws {{InvalidOperationException}}.
* A counter pin cannot also be opened through the controller.
*Tests:* {{LibgpiodEdgeCounterTests.Line_settings_enums_match_gpiod_h}}; GPIO behaviour via {{FakeGpioPins}} in {{IoBoardHardwareSystemTests}}. (Real libgpiod is not unit-tested.)
