*Public contract:*
```csharp
internal static class HelperLocator {
    public const string PioDevice = "/dev/pio0";
    public static string Resolve(string name, string? configured, string? nativeDir);
    public static bool PioAvailable();     // File.Exists("/dev/pio0")
}
internal sealed class HelperProcess : IDisposable {
    public string ReadyLine { get; }
    public bool IsRunning { get; }
    public static HelperProcess Start(string exe, IEnumerable<string> args, TimeSpan readyTimeout);
    public void Command(string command, TimeSpan? timeout = null);
}
```
*Behaviour & rules:*
# {{Resolve}}: candidates = [configured (if not blank)], {{<nativeDir ?? AppContext.BaseDirectory/native>/<name>}}, {{/usr/local/bin/<name>}}; return the first existing file, else the first candidate (so the error names it).
# {{Start}}: exe missing -> {{FileNotFoundException("{exe} not built - run native/build-pio-helpers.sh")}}. Start with redirected stdin/stdout/stderr, no shell, args via {{ArgumentList}}. Read one stdout line with {{readyTimeout}}; if none or it does not start with "READY": kill the process tree, read stderr for up to 1 s, throw {{InvalidOperationException("{fileName}: {line or stderr, trimmed, or 'no READY'}")}}. {{ReadyLine}} = trimmed READY line.
# {{Command}}: not running -> {{InvalidOperationException("helper process is not running")}}; under an IO lock write {{command + '\n'}}, flush, read one reply line (default timeout 1 s, {{TimeoutException("no reply from helper")}} on timeout); reply trimmed must be exactly "OK" else {{InvalidOperationException("helper '{first token}': {reply or 'no reply'}")}}.
# {{Dispose}} (idempotent): if alive write "Q\n", wait 2000 ms, else kill tree; on any exception kill; finally dispose the Process.
# {{pio_servo <gpio> [--inverted] [--period-us N (2000..65000, default 20000)] [--pio IDX (default 0)] [--sm N (default 3; -1 any free)] [--test <pulse_us> <hold_ms>]}}. Program (clkdiv 200 on the 200 MHz RP1 clock = 1 us per instruction, 1 side-set pin): {{pull block side IDLE; out x,16 side IDLE; out y,16 side IDLE; jmp x--,3 side ACTIVE; jmp y--,4 side IDLE}}; word = (y<<16)|(x&0xFFFF), x = pulse-1, y = period-pulse-4. Idle level = inverted ? HIGH : LOW. Keeps the 4-deep TX FIFO topped up every 20 ms while driving. Commands: {{P <us>}} (pulse must be >=100 and pulse+8 <= period, else {{ERR pulse out of range}}; {{ERR bad pulse}} for non-positive/garbage; a new width clears the FIFO so it applies within one period), {{R}} release (clear FIFO, pulse in flight finishes, line idles), {{Q}} quit; each replied {{OK}} / {{ERR <reason>}}; unknown -> {{ERR unknown command}}. Prints once {{READY gpio=<n> sm=<n> inverted=<0|1> period_us=<n>}}. stdin HUP -> release and exit. Teardown waits one period + 1 ms before disabling the SM.
# {{pio_rgb <gpio> <count> [--order RGB|GRB (default RGB)] [--pio IDX] [--sm N (default 2)] [--test RRGGBB]}}. WS2811 program, 10 PIO cycles per bit at 8 MHz (clkdiv = 200e6/(800e3*10) = 25.0), T1=3, T2=4, T3=3 ('0' = 0.375 us high / 0.875 low; '1' = 0.875 / 0.375); shift left, autopull 24 bits, TX FIFO joined (8 deep); idle LOW. Commands: {{F <hex>}} exactly 6*count hex chars in RRGGBB per LED (helper reorders to GRB when {{--order GRB}}; errors {{frame length mismatch}}, {{bad hex}}), {{O}} all off, {{Q}} quit (strip left as is); over-long line -> {{ERR line too long}}. After each frame wait for FIFO empty then 300 us latch. Prints {{READY gpio=<n> sm=<n> count=<n> order=<RGB|GRB>}}.
# Build: {{build-pio-helpers.sh}} compiles each helper with {{gcc -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Wno-unused-parameter -DLIBRARY_BUILD=1 -I$SRC/include}} against piolib sources {{piolib.c pio_rp1.c library_piochips.c}} from raspberrypi/utils (git clone to {{/tmp/rpi-utils}} unless {{PIOLIB_SRC}} set); {{install}} arg copies to {{/usr/local/bin}}.
*Configuration:* {{HardwareOptions.NativeDir}} (host passes {{SCURE_NATIVE_DIR}}), {{servo.pio_helper}}.
*Acceptance criteria:*
* {{Resolve}} prefers the configured path, then native dir, then /usr/local/bin, and returns the first candidate when none exists.
* A helper that does not print READY within the timeout is killed and {{Start}} throws {{InvalidOperationException}}.
* A reply other than "OK" makes {{Command}} throw with the command's first token in the message.
*Tests:* none directly in the existing suite (helpers need /dev/pio0); drivers are tested through {{FakeServoDriver}} / {{FakeRgbDriver}}.
*Reference (source):* {{src/SCureBox.Hardware/Helpers/HelperLocator.cs}}, {{Helpers/HelperProcess.cs}}, {{native/pio_servo.c}}, {{native/pio_rgb.c}}, {{native/build-pio-helpers.sh}}, {{native/linux-arm64/README.txt}}

