*Behaviour & rules:*
# {{PulseUs(angle)}}: clamp 0..180; a = 180 - angle (logical flip of the linkage); pulse = round(500 + a/180*1900). 0 -> 2400, 90 -> 1450, 180 -> 500, -10 -> 2400, 200 -> 500.
# {{DutyPercent(pulse, inverted)}} = pulse/20000*100, inverted -> 100 - that (1450 -> 7.25 / 92.75). The electrical Q16 inversion is separate from the logical flip.
# {{PioServoDriver.Start}}: {{/dev/pio0}} missing -> {{FileNotFoundException("/dev/pio0 missing (RP1 PIO: Pi 5 / CM5 kernel only)")}}; spawn helper with args {{[gpio, "--inverted" if inverted]}}, READY timeout 3 s. {{Drive(p)}} -> {{Command("P {p}")}}; {{Release}} -> {{Command("R")}}; Dispose disposes the helper.
# {{SoftwarePwmServoDriver}}: the {{SoftwarePwmChannel}} exists only while driven (its precision-timer thread busy-waits a core). {{Drive}}: duty fraction = DutyPercent/100; if no channel: close the pin if open, create {{new SoftwarePwmChannel(gpio, 50, duty, usePrecisionTimer: true, controller, shouldDispose: false)}} and {{Start()}}; else set {{DutyCycle}}. {{Release}}: stop + dispose the channel; open the pin as output if not open; write idle level (inverted ? High : Low). Dispose = Release.
# {{DamperServo.Create}}: driver = {{cfg.Driver}} trimmed lower; for "auto" or "pio": resolve helper ({{HelperLocator.Resolve("pio_servo", cfg.PioHelper, nativeDir)}}) and {{PioServoDriver.Start}}; for "auto" any exception logs a warning and falls back; for "pio" the exception propagates. Otherwise (or fallback) {{softwareFactory()}}. Log the driver choice. Returns {{new DamperServo(driver, cfg.SettleSec, time)}}.
# {{Goto(angle, force)}}: clamp; under lock: if !force and holding and same angle -> return (skip); else cancel the release timer, {{Drive(PulseUs)}}, LastAngle = angle, Holding = true; if settle > 0 start a one-shot {{TimeProvider.CreateTimer}} after settle that calls {{Release()}}. settle <= 0 = hold forever. Returns the applied angle.
# {{Release()}}: Holding = false; driver.Release() with exceptions swallowed. After release a same-angle Goto re-drives (recovers a stalled servo). Dispose cancels the timer and disposes the driver.
*Configuration:* {{servo.gpio}} (8), {{servo.driver}} ("auto" | "pio" | "lgpio"), {{servo.signal_inverted}} (true), {{servo.settle_sec}} (1.5), {{servo.pio_helper}} (null).
*Acceptance criteria:*
* Goto(90) with settle 1.5 -> pulses [1450], Holding; repeat Goto(90) skipped; no release at 1.4 s, release at 1.5 s; Goto(90) after release re-drives; Goto(0) -> 2400 and restarts the timer (second release 1.5 s later).
* Settle 0 -> no release after 5 minutes.
*Tests:* {{ServoTests}} (Pulse_math_flips_the_logical_angle theory, Software_pwm_duty_and_electrical_inversion, Damper_settles_then_releases_and_skips_a_repeat_while_holding, Damper_with_zero_settle_holds_forever) with {{FakeTimeProvider}}.
