*Behaviour & rules:*
# Heartbeat line {{"<Environment.TickCount64 ms> <pid>\n"}} (monotonic since boot); {{TryReadTick}} returns the first whitespace token parsed as long, null if missing/unparsable/IO error. {{Delete}} swallows IO/permission errors (clean stop = watchdog disarms). /run is tmpfs.
# Trip record: {{TryRead}} -> null if missing or first token not a long; CutOk = (no second token) or second token == "ok".
# {{SafetyCut.Cut()}}: try {{new Pca9685(pcaBus)}} (writes MODE1 0x20, MODE2 0x04) - failure -> Failed "PCA9685 not answering ({msg})" and skip the channels. For ch 6 (label "heater (PCA ch 6)") then LED channels ordered by channel 11, 12, 13, 14 (label "{LED} DIM (PCA ch {ch})"): write {{IntendedRegisters(ch, 0)}} via {{SetPwm}}, read the 4 bytes back at 0x55; match -> Done "{label} off", else Failed "{label} read back on=0x{on:X4} off=0x{off:X4}"; exceptions -> Failed "{label} ({msg})". Then for each SSR GPIO: {{gpioLow(gpio)}} -> Done "LED supply SSR GPIO{gpio} LOW" / Failed "LED supply SSR GPIO{gpio} ({msg})". Every step is attempted. Fans (ch 0-5) are never written.
# {{PinctrlLow(gpio)}}: run {{pinctrl set {gpio} op dl}}, then {{pinctrl lev {gpio}}}; output trimmed must be "0" else {{IOException("pinctrl reads level '{x}' after set LOW")}}. Process helper: 5 s timeout (kill + IOException), non-zero exit -> IOException with stderr.
# {{Run(args)}}: defaults timeout 20, heartbeat = {{HeartbeatFile.ConfiguredPath() ?? DefaultPath}}, components = env {{SCURE_COMPONENTS}} ?? {{/etc/scurebox/components.json}}. Args: {{--timeout <sec>}} (>0, invariant), {{--heartbeat <file>}}, {{--components <json>}}, {{--cut-now}}; anything else -> stderr usage {{"usage: scurebox --watchdog [--timeout <sec>] [--heartbeat <file>] [--components <json>] [--cut-now]"}}, exit 2. SSR pins from {{HardwareConfig(components)}} (or {{FromJson("{}")}} if the file is missing) {{LedPower.Ssr450Gpio}}, {{Ssr405Gpio}}; on exception default 16/20 with a stderr note. Opens {{SystemDeviceI2cBus(0)}}; {{SafetyCut(bus, PinctrlLow, distinct SSR pins)}}.
# {{--cut-now}}: one cut, log "manual cut: heaters + UV LEDs OFF (verified)" or "manual cut: INCOMPLETE" plus the off/FAILED lists; exit 0 if Ok else 1.
# Loop (until Ctrl+C / process exit; poll 500 ms): {{WatchdogMonitor(timeout, 5).Step(TryReadTick(heartbeat), Environment.TickCount64)}}: Armed -> "[WATCHDOG] firmware heartbeat present - armed"; Disarmed -> "...firmware stopped cleanly (heartbeat removed) - disarmed"; Tripped -> cut, log "TRIPPED - firmware silent for {age:0.0} s|no heartbeat: heaters + UV LEDs OFF (verified)|cut INCOMPLETE" + lists, then {{WatchdogTripFile.Write(PathFor(heartbeat), UtcNow, report.Ok)}} (IO errors logged); Recut (every 5 s while silent) -> cut, log only if incomplete; Recovered -> "...firmware heartbeat back - the firmware is in control again". A heartbeat already stale when the watchdog starts trips too. Startup line: "[WATCHDOG] watching {hb}: heaters + UV LEDs off after {t} s without a firmware heartbeat (SSR GPIO 16/20)". All lines prefixed "[WATCHDOG]", stdout flushed. Returns 0.
*Configuration:* env {{SCURE_HEARTBEAT_FILE}} (path or "off"), {{SCURE_COMPONENTS}}; components.json {{led_power.ssr_450nm}} / {{ssr_405nm}}; CLI args above.
*Acceptance criteria:*
* Cut with heater SSR on, LEDs dimmed and fan 0 running: report Ok, ch 6/11/12/13/14 read {{00 00 00 10}}, ch0 untouched (no write to it), gpioLow called with [16, 20], 7 Done entries.
* PCA NAK: Failed contains "PCA9685 not answering", SSRs still switched low.
* Heater write dropped: Failed starts "heater (PCA ch 6) read back"; failing GPIO20 -> Failed mentions "GPIO20" and the message; Done contains "LED supply SSR GPIO16 LOW".
* Heartbeat round trip: missing -> null; write 123456789 -> read back; overwrite; delete -> null; "garbage" -> null.
*Tests:* {{SafetyCutTests}} (Cut_switches_the_heater_and_the_four_LED_DIM_channels_full_off_and_the_SSRs_low_and_leaves_the_fans, A_dead_PCA_is_reported_but_the_SSRs_are_still_switched_low, A_register_that_does_not_read_back_off_and_a_failing_GPIO_are_failures, Heartbeat_file_round_trip_and_delete). WatchdogMonitor state machine is tested in Domain.
*Reference (source):* {{src/SCureBox.Hardware/Safety/HeartbeatFile.cs}}, {{Safety/WatchdogTripFile.cs}}, {{Safety/SafetyCut.cs}}, {{Safety/OutputWatchdog.cs}}, {{src/SCureBox.Domain/Control/WatchdogMonitor.cs}}, {{tests/SCureBox.Hardware.Tests/SafetyCutTests.cs}}, {{docs/02-hardware-map.md}} (Output watchdog)

