```
*Behaviour & rules:*
# {{SimulationReason}}: "ForceSimulation" if forced; "SCURE_SIMULATE=1" if the env asks; "not Linux"; "/dev/i2c-0 missing"; then probe {{Pca9685.ProbeMode1(new SystemDeviceI2cBus(0))}} (disposed) - exception -> "PCA9685 not answering at 0x55 ({msg})"; else null (use the real board).
# {{Create}}: reason null -> try OpenBoard, log info "hardware: real IO board (io_controller) on /dev/i2c-0 + /dev/i2c-1"; any exception -> reason "IO board open failed: {msg}", log error. Otherwise log warning "hardware: SIMULATION ({reason})" and return {{new SimulatedHardwareSystem(config, timeProvider)}}.
# OpenBoard: chip = {{options.GpioChip ?? SystemDeviceGpioPins.DetectRp1Chip()}}; bus0 = {{SystemDeviceI2cBus(0)}}, bus1 = {{SystemDeviceI2cBus(1)}}, gpio = {{SystemDeviceGpioPins(chip)}}. Servo factory: {{DamperServo.Create(config.Servo, options.NativeDir, () => new SoftwarePwmServoDriver(new GpioController(LibgpiodDrivers.Create(chip)), cfg.Gpio, cfg.SignalInverted), time, log)}}. RGB factory: {{PioRgbDriver.Start(HelperLocator.Resolve("pio_rgb", null, options.NativeDir), rgb.Gpio, rgb.Count, rgb.Order)}} and log its READY line. Construct {{IoBoardHardwareSystem(bus0, bus1, gpio, config, time, null, ServoFactory, RgbFactory, log)}} then {{StartupSafe()}} - an exception there is logged ("startup safe state incomplete") and the board is still returned.
# {{AddSCureBoxHardware}}: null args -> {{ArgumentNullException}}; if not forced but the env asks, set {{ForceSimulation = true}}. Register singletons: the {{HardwareOptions}} instance; {{IHardwareConfig}} = {{new HardwareConfig(options.ComponentsPath, sp.GetService<TimeProvider>(), logger)}}; {{Safety.OutputFreeze}}; {{IHardwareSystem}} = {{new FreezableHardwareSystem(HardwareSystemFactory.Create(options, config, loggerFactory, sp.GetService<TimeProvider>()), freeze)}}. Logger factory falls back to {{NullLoggerFactory.Instance}}.
*Configuration:* env {{SCURE_SIMULATE}} (1/true/yes), {{HardwareOptions}} (ComponentsPath, ForceSimulation, NativeDir, GpioChip); host env {{SCURE_NATIVE_DIR}} -> NativeDir (Origin package: {{/opt/data/scurebox/native}}).
*Acceptance criteria:*
* On Windows / without {{/dev/i2c-0}} / with {{SCURE_SIMULATE=1}} the resolved {{IHardwareSystem}} is a {{FreezableHardwareSystem}} whose {{Inner}} is {{SimulatedHardwareSystem}} and {{Source}} is "simulation".
* {{SimulationReason}} returns the exact strings above in that precedence.
* An exception while opening the board falls back to the simulation instead of failing start-up.
* {{IHardwareConfig}}, {{OutputFreeze}} and {{IHardwareSystem}} resolve as singletons (same instance each time).
*Tests:* none in {{SCureBox.Hardware.Tests}}; recommended: HardwareOptions env parsing and DI resolution tests (simulation path on a dev machine).
*Reference (source):* {{src/SCureBox.Hardware/HardwareOptions.cs}}, {{src/SCureBox.Hardware/HardwareSystemFactory.cs}}, {{src/SCureBox.Hardware/HardwareServiceCollectionExtensions.cs}}, {{src/SCureBox.Api/ScureApiHost.cs}} (registration call)

