On-disk files (all in {{DataDir}}):
||file||content||
| {{user_materials.json}} | {{Material[]}} (indented) — user programs |
| {{print_history.json}} | {{PrintLog[]}} |
| {{cure_history.json}} | {{CureLog[]}} newest first, each with its {{telemetry[]}} |
| {{cure_reports.json}} | {{{ "<extId>": CureReport{content, summary, format} }}} |
| {{phase_timings.json}} | {{PhaseTiming[]}} newest last |
Presets: {{ConfigDir/presets.json}} ({{Material[]}}), read-only.
*Behaviour & rules:*
# Materials: presets load lazily ({{Lazy<>}}) from {{PresetsPath}}; every preset is returned with {{IsPreset = true}}. Missing file → {{LogWarning("[DATA] presets file missing: {Path}")}} and empty list; unreadable → warning + empty. User programs = {{user_materials.json}}, replaced as a whole ({{ReplaceUserMaterials}} saves indented). {{Find(id)}}: presets first, then user materials. Preset JSON keeps its wire shape (round-trips the {{steps}} fields as read).
# Print history: {{ReplaceAll}} replaces and saves the whole list; {{GetAll}} returns a copy.
# Cure runs — constructor: load {{cure_history.json}} (fallback empty), load {{cure_reports.json}} (own tolerant loader; warning {{"[DATA] read failed (cure_reports.json)"}}). Every run whose {{Status == "running"}} is rewritten to {{"error"}} (a power-cut run can never finish). Then {{Trim()}}. If anything changed, save the history.
# {{Start(extId, start)}}: if the id is not present, insert at index 0 a {{CureLog{ Id=extId, MaterialName, Steps, StepsCompleted=0, StartedAt=local now "yyyy-MM-ddTHH:mm:ss" (invariant), EndedAt=null, Duration=null, Status="running", Phases, TargetTemp, SerialNumber, Telemetry=new list }}} then {{Trim()}}. Always save (idempotent: a second Start with same id does not add a row).
# {{Trim()}}: keep the first {{KeepRuns}} (25) runs; for removed runs drop their in-memory telemetry and their entries in {{cure_reports.json}} (rewritten only if one was removed).
# {{AddTelemetry}}: unknown id → false. Append sample; increment an unflushed counter; when it reaches {{TelemetryFlushEvery}} (15) save history and reset counter. (Power cut loses ≤ last few samples, never the run.)
# {{Finish}}: unknown → false. {{duration = floor((localNow - parse(StartedAt, "yyyy-MM-ddTHH:mm:ss")).TotalSeconds)}} (keep previous if unparsable); set {{Status=finish.Status}}, {{EndedAt=stamp(now)}}, {{StepsCompleted = finish.StepsCompleted ?? previous}}, {{SensorIssues}}, {{FanIssues}}, {{Alerts = finish.Alerts ?? previous}}, {{Duration}}. Save, reset unflushed counter.
# {{SaveReport(extId, report)}}: store under {{extId}} (no check that the run exists), rewrite {{cure_reports.json}}, return {{extId}}. {{GetReport}} returns it or null.
# {{Delete(extId)}}: false if unknown or {{Status=="running"}}; else remove run + telemetry + report, save. {{DeleteAll()}}: remove every non-running run, return their ids.
# {{Flush()}}: save history now. {{GetHistory()}} returns deep-ish copies (telemetry list copied).
# Phase timings: {{Append}} adds at end, saves, returns new count.
# All public methods lock {{Sync}}.
*Configuration:* {{ConfigDir/presets.json}}.
*Acceptance criteria:*
* Start twice with the same id → 1 run; new runs appear first.
* After 26 starts only 25 runs remain; the oldest's report is gone from {{cure_reports.json}}.
* 14 telemetry samples do not rewrite the file, the 15th does; {{Flush()}} writes immediately.
* Reloading a file that has a {{running}} run yields {{error}}.
* {{Finish}} with {{StepsCompleted=null}} keeps the previous value; duration computed in whole seconds.
* A running run is never deleted by {{Delete}}/{{DeleteAll}}.
* Corrupt {{cure_history.json}} → empty history, no exception.
*Tests:* {{Persistence/JsonCureRunStoreTests}} (Start_is_idempotent_and_inserts_newest_first, Delete_removes_a_finished_run_with_its_report_but_never_a_running_one, History_keeps_the_newest_25_runs, Telemetry_flushes_every_15_samples_and_on_flush, Finish_computes_duration_and_records_issues, Finish_without_steps_completed_keeps_the_previous_value, Runs_left_running_become_error_on_reload, Report_round_trip, Corrupt_history_file_starts_empty) with {{FakeTimeProvider}}; {{JsonMaterialStoreTests}} (Presets_come_from_config_presets_json, User_materials_are_replaced_as_a_whole_and_persist, Missing_presets_file_gives_an_empty_list, Preset_json_keeps_the_wire_shape); {{JsonPrintHistoryStoreTests}} (Replace_all_persists_and_reloads); {{JsonPhaseTimingStoreTests}} (Append_returns_the_count_and_keeps_order).
*Reference (source):* {{src/SCureBox.Application/Contracts/IStores.cs}}, {{src/SCureBox.Application/Persistence/Json{Material,PrintHistory,CureRun,PhaseTiming}Store.cs}}, {{src/SCureBox.Domain/Models/History.cs}}, {{tests/SCureBox.Application.Tests/Persistence/*}}

