* {{cure_run_telemetry(id BIGSERIAL PK, cure_run_id→cure_runs ON DELETE CASCADE NOT NULL, t INTEGER NOT NULL, chamber_temp NUMERIC, uv_on BOOLEAN, uv_type TEXT, led_right, led_left, led_door, led_back NUMERIC, recorded_at DEFAULT now())}} + {{fan_rpm JSONB}}; {{ix_telemetry_run(cure_run_id, t)}}
* {{cure_reports(id, cure_run_id→cure_runs CASCADE NOT NULL, format TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'html', content TEXT, summary JSONB, generated_at DEFAULT now())}}; {{ix_reports_run}}
* Views: {{v_materials(id = COALESCE(ext_id,id::text), name, "isPreset", "createdAt", steps = COALESCE(cp.parameters->'steps','[]'), "totalDuration" = COALESCE((parameters->>'totalDuration')::int,0))}} LEFT JOIN cure_profiles on material_id, ORDER BY is_preset DESC, created_at. {{v_print_history(id, "printName"=COALESCE(p.name,'Print'), "materialName" (via jobs→materials), "printerName"=printers.serial_number, date=COALESCE(p.start_time, cr.started_at), duration=EPOCH(end-start) of print else of cure run, status=COALESCE(cr.status,p.status), steps=cr.steps, "csvFile"=cp.parameters->>'csvFile')}} ORDER BY date DESC. {{v_cure_history(id, "materialName", steps, "stepsCompleted", "startedAt", "endedAt", duration=EPOCH(ended-started)::int, status, phases, "targetTemp", "sensorIssues", "fanIssues", "serialNumber"=cure_boxes.serial_number, telemetry = jsonb_agg({t, chamberTemp, uvOn, uvType, ledTemps:{right,left,door,back}, fanRpm} ORDER BY t) or '[]', alerts=run_alerts)}} ORDER BY started_at DESC.
* {{seed_presets.sql}}: per preset {{WITH ins AS (INSERT INTO materials (ext_id, name, is_preset) VALUES ('preset-<Name>', '<Name>', TRUE) ON CONFLICT (ext_id) DO NOTHING RETURNING id) INSERT INTO cure_profiles (material_id, parameters) SELECT id, '<{"steps":[...],"totalDuration":N,"isPreset":true}>'::jsonb FROM ins;}} (generated from presets.json; e.g. {{preset-ST45}} totalDuration 79).
*Behaviour & rules:*
# {{Normalize}}: if the string does not start with {{postgres://}}/{{postgresql://}} (case-insensitive) parse as key=value with {{NpgsqlConnectionStringBuilder}}, and if {{Timeout == 15}} (default) set it to 5. URL form: Host, Port (5432 when default), Database = path trimmed of '/', Timeout=5, Username/Password from userinfo (URL-unescaped, split on first ':'), query {{sslmode=X}} → {{"SSL Mode"}}.
# {{TryInitialize}}: open a connection; resolve schema dir = {{options.SchemaDir}} if set, else first existing of {{<app>/db}}, {{<app>/deploy/db}}, then {{<dir>/deploy/db}} walking up from {{AppContext.BaseDirectory}} (must contain {{schema.sql}}). None → {{LogWarning("[DB] schema.sql not found - using the database as-is")}} and still succeed. Execute {{schema.sql}} then {{seed_presets.sql}} (each only if it exists; {{CommandTimeout = 60}}). Catch {{NpgsqlException, IOException, InvalidOperationException, TimeoutException, ArgumentException}} → false + message. Never throws.
# {{StoreSelector}}: if {{database.IsConfigured}}: construct {{PostgresDb}}, run initializer; success → Postgres stores, {{UsingPostgres = true}}, log {{"[DB] data store: POSTGRES (schema ensured)"}}. Failure → {{"[DB] Postgres unavailable ({Error}) - falling back to JSON files"}}, dispose. {{ArgumentException/FormatException/UriFormatException}} from a bad string → {{"[DB] bad connection string"}} warning. Otherwise JSON stores (PLAT-02). Decision is sticky; {{Dispose()}} disposes the data source.
# {{PostgresMaterialStore}}: presets = {{SELECT * FROM v_materials WHERE "isPreset"}}, user = {{NOT "isPreset"}}, Find = {{WHERE id = $1}}. Row → {{Material{Id, Name, IsPreset, CreatedAt=GetIsoStamp, Steps=GetJson<List<CureStep>> ?? [], TotalDuration ?? 0}}}. {{ReplaceUserMaterials}} in one transaction: per material {{INSERT INTO materials(ext_id,name,is_preset) VALUES($1,$2,FALSE) ON CONFLICT(ext_id) DO UPDATE SET name=EXCLUDED.name RETURNING id}} (empty name → "Untitled"); {{DELETE FROM cure_profiles WHERE material_id=$1}}; insert profile {{parameters = {steps, totalDuration, isPreset:false}}}; then prune {{DELETE FROM materials WHERE is_preset=FALSE AND ext_id IS NOT NULL AND NOT (ext_id = ANY($1))}} (or all user materials when the list is empty). Presets untouched.
# {{PostgresPrintHistoryStore.GetAll}}: from {{v_print_history}}; defaults printName "Print", status "completed", date via {{GetLocalStamp}}. {{ReplaceAll}} (transaction): per log → {{UpsertPrinter(serial)}} ({{INSERT .. ON CONFLICT(serial_number) DO UPDATE .. RETURNING id}}, null when empty), {{FindOrCreateMaterial(name)}} ({{SELECT id FROM materials WHERE name=$1 ORDER BY is_preset DESC LIMIT 1}}, else insert), start={{ParseStamp(Date)}}, end=start+floor(Duration) s; upsert {{prints}} by ext_id returning {{id, job_id}}; if no job and a material: insert {{jobs(material_id)}} and link; upsert {{cure_runs(ext_id=log.Id, print_id, steps, started_at, ended_at, status)}}. Then prune {{cure_runs}} and {{prints}} rows whose ext_id not in the list. NOTE: {{PrintLog.NfcTag}} is not persisted in Postgres (OPEN QUESTION: intended?).
# {{PostgresCureRunStore}}: {{GetHistory}} from {{v_cure_history}} (status default "running"). {{Start}} (transaction): upsert {{cure_boxes(serial_number)}} when serial given; {{FindOrCreateMaterial(MaterialName)}} when given (linkage is via the print, so not stored on the run); {{INSERT INTO cure_runs (ext_id, cure_box_id, steps, steps_completed=0, target_temp, phases, started_at=now(), status='running') ON CONFLICT(ext_id) DO UPDATE ...status='running'}}; then trim {{DELETE FROM cure_runs WHERE id IN (SELECT id FROM cure_runs ORDER BY started_at DESC NULLS LAST OFFSET 25)}} (telemetry/reports cascade). {{AddTelemetry}}: run id lookup (false when unknown); insert telemetry row with {{t = round(sample.T)}}, led temps from {{LedTemps["right"/"left"/"door"/"back"]}}, {{fan_rpm}} jsonb or null. Only these columns are stored (timing-diagram fields are lost in Postgres). {{Finish}}: {{UPDATE cure_runs SET status, ended_at=now(), steps_completed=COALESCE($2,steps_completed), sensor_issues, fan_issues, run_alerts=COALESCE($6,run_alerts) WHERE ext_id=$5}}; true when a row changed. {{SaveReport}}: create a minimal run ({{status 'completed'}}) when the id is unknown; insert {{cure_reports(cure_run_id, format, content, summary)}} (summary raw JSON or NULL when undefined/null); returns the *report row UUID* (differs from JSON store which returns extId). {{GetReport}}: newest by {{generated_at}}; format default "html", content default "". {{Delete}}: {{DELETE ... WHERE ext_id=$1 AND status <> 'running'}}. {{DeleteAll}}: {{DELETE ... WHERE status <> 'running' RETURNING ext_id}}. {{Flush}}: no-op.
*Configuration:* {{DatabaseOptions.ConnectionString}} (env {{DATABASE_URL}}), {{DatabaseOptions.SchemaDir}}.
*Acceptance criteria:*
* {{Normalize("postgresql://u:p%40ss@h:6543/db?sslmode=require")}} yields Host=h, Port=6543, Database=db, Username=u, Password=p@ss, SSL Mode=Require, Timeout=5; key=value strings get Timeout 5 unless one was set.
* An unreachable database leaves {{UsingPostgres == false}} and JSON stores in use, without throwing.
* Against a real server (only when {{SCURE_TEST_DATABASE_URL}} is set): start/telemetry/finish/report/history round-trip; re-running schema.sql is harmless.
*Tests:* {{Persistence/PostgresSmokeTests}} (Connection_string_normalisation_accepts_urls_and_key_values, Unreachable_database_falls_back_to_json_stores, Round_trip_against_a_real_server_when_configured — skipped unless env {{SCURE_TEST_DATABASE_URL}}).
*Reference (source):* {{src/SCureBox.Application/Persistence/{PostgresDb,IDatabaseInitializer,PostgresDatabaseInitializer,PostgresMaterialStore,PostgresPrintHistoryStore,PostgresCureRunStore,StoreSelector}.cs}}, {{deploy/db/schema.sql}}, {{deploy/db/seed_presets.sql}}

