```
*Behaviour & rules:*
# Supervisor URL: ctor {{url}} ?? env {{SCURE_SUPERVISOR_URL}}. *Off* when the value is {{"off"}} (case-insensitive) or when not Linux and no URL is given (an unrelated :8080 service on a PC must not be mistaken for it). HttpClient timeout 20 s; base address = given URL or DefaultUrl.
# Endpoints: {{IsAvailable}} = {{GET /api/status}} success within 1.5 s (off → false). {{FindInstallers}} = {{GET /api/external-storage/find-app-installers}} → JSON array of {{{name, version, path}}} (items without {{path}} skipped; errors → empty, warning {{"[UPDATE] supervisor: installers not readable"}}). {{Install}} = {{POST /api/application/install}} body {{{"path": "<path>"}}}; non-success → error = problem-details {{detail}} ?? {{title}} ?? {{"HTTP <code>"}}. {{GetApplication}} = {{GET /api/application}} → {{ParseApplication}}. {{NetworkTimeEnabled}} = {{GET /api/machine/clock}} → {{ntpEnabled}} bool or null (off/err/missing → null). {{SetNetworkTime}} = {{POST /api/machine/clock}} {{{"ntpEnabled": on}}}; off → false with error {{"no supervisor"}}.
# {{ParseApplication(root)}}: {{{state, version, install:{state?, exitCode?, error?}}}}; InstallFailed when {{install.error}} non-blank, or {{install.state}} contains "fail"/"error"/"cancel" (case-insensitive), or numeric {{exitCode != 0}}. InstallError = blank → null. Missing state → "".
# {{SystemService.SetDateTime(date, time)}}: date must match {{^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$}}, time {{^\d{2}:\d{2}(:\d{2})?$}}, else Fail("Invalid date/time format") (no code) *and network time is not touched*. Valid: switch network time OFF first — via {{supervisor.SetNetworkTime(false)}}; if that is not true and on Linux, {{timedatectl set-ntp false}} (15 s). Off-Linux: remember NTP off, Success "Clock set simulated (<date> <time>)". Linux: {{timedatectl set-time "<date> <HH:MM:00 or HH:MM:SS>"}} (15 s); failure → Fail(stderr or "set-time failed"); success "Clock set to <date> <time>".
# {{NetworkTimeEnabled()}}: supervisor answer when non-null; else off-Linux simulated flag (initially *true*); else {{timedatectl show -p NTP --value}} == "yes" (10 s).
# {{SetNetworkTime(on)}}: log {{"[SYSTEM] network time synchronisation ON|OFF"}}. Supervisor present and {{SetNetworkTime}} ok → Success "Network time on|off". If refused with a reason other than "no supervisor" → warning and fall back. Off-Linux → simulated flag, "Network time on|off simulated". Linux → {{timedatectl set-ntp true|false}}; fail → Fail(stderr or "set-ntp failed"). Rationale (SRS OI-54): units have no RTC; a clock left manual stays months behind and HTTPS fails ("certificate is not yet valid").
*Configuration:* env {{SCURE_SUPERVISOR_URL}} (URL or {{off}}).
*Acceptance criteria:*
* A fresh (simulated) machine reports network time enabled; a valid manual clock set turns it off; {{SetNetworkTime(true)}} turns it back on; a malformed date leaves it unchanged.
* With a fake supervisor: SetNetworkTime goes through {{POST /api/machine/clock}}; manual clock sends {{ntpEnabled:false}} to the supervisor; a silent supervisor (null) falls back to the machine's own setting.
* {{ParseApplication}} flags failure for {{install.exitCode: 1}}, {{install.state: "Failed"}}, or a non-empty error.
*Tests:* {{Platform/NetworkTimeTests}} (A_machine_keeps_its_clock_synchronised_until_something_says_otherwise, Setting_the_clock_by_hand_switches_network_time_off, Network_time_can_be_switched_back_on_after_a_manual_clock, A_malformed_date_leaves_network_time_alone, Network_time_is_set_through_the_supervisor_so_it_survives_a_restart, A_manual_clock_switches_network_time_off_in_the_supervisor, A_silent_supervisor_falls_back_to_the_machines_own_setting); {{SupervisorUpdateTests.The_application_reply_is_read_leniently}}.
*Reference (source):* {{src/SCureBox.Application/Platform/{SystemService,SupervisorClient}.cs}}

