*{{.scu}} format:* uncompressed tar (PAX) containing {{<name>.tar.gz}} and {{<name>.tar.gz.sig}}, where {{<name>}} = output file name without {{.scu}}. Signature = RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 over SHA-256 of the exact {{.tar.gz}} bytes ({{openssl dgst -sha256 -sign}} compatible). Inner tar.gz (PAX, gzip optimal) = directory {{<name>/}} with the source tree (dirs and files sorted ordinal; modes: dirs and {{*.sh}} 0755, other files 0644); must contain {{manifest.json}} ({{{"version": "...", ...}}}) and {{install.sh}}.
*Behaviour & rules:*
# Public key lookup (first existing): {{<app>/keys/scure-update.pub}}, {{/opt/scurebox/keys/scure-update.pub}}, {{/opt/scure/keys/scure-update.pub}}, then {{<dir>/deploy/keys/scure-update.pub}} walking up from the app dir. PEM SubjectPublicKeyInfo or PKCS#1. Private key is never on the device (builder only).
# {{ExtractAndVerify}}: extract outer tar to workDir; first {{*.tar.gz}} and {{*.sig}} required else "Invalid package structure"; no key → "Public key not found"; {{CryptographicException}} → "Invalid signature: <msg>"; false → "Invalid signature". Then gunzip+untar payload into workDir; UpdateDir = first subdirectory (ordinal) holding {{manifest.json}}, else workDir if it holds one, else "No manifest found in package". IO/InvalidData/Format errors → message.
# {{NewestPackage(usb)}}: {{*.scu}} in the USB root plus {{<usb>/scure-update/*.scu}}, newest {{LastWriteTimeUtc}} first, ties by path ordinal.
# Work dir: {{<workRoot or temp>/scure-update-<guid N>}}, always deleted (finally).
# {{FindPackage}} (no supervisor): no USB → {{{Code 9081, "No USB drive found"}}}; none → {{{Code 9087, "No .scu update file found on USB"}}}; IO → 9086.
# {{Manifest}}: package + SHA-256 of the {{.scu}}; version = manifest {{version}} when it verifies, else the file name.
# {{RunUpdate}} ({{.scu}} path) step list, each marked running→ok/error in order: {{find_usb}} (fail 9081 NoUsbMessage) → {{find_package}} (fail 9087 NoPackageMessage; IO 9086) → {{verify_signature}} (a failure whose message contains "signature" or "key" fails here: "Verification failed: <msg>", 9086; other extract failures mark verify ok and fail {{extract}}) → {{extract}} ok → {{manifest}} (version or "unknown") → {{install_pre}} ({{bash install.sh --pre}}, 300 s) → {{install_post}} ({{--post}}, 300 s); a non-zero exit runs {{install.sh --rollback}} (120 s) and fails with "Failed at 'Pre-install backup'|'Installing update': <stderr>" code 9086 + Version → {{cleanup}} (delete work dir; Linux {{umount <usb>}} 10 s) → {{{Ok, Version, Message "Updated to version <v>"}}}.
# {{BashScriptRunner}}: {{bash <script> <arg>}}; off-Linux, exit -1 not caused by a timeout → simulated {{(0, "simulated: install.sh <arg>", "")}}.
# Supervisor path (used by all three methods whenever {{supervisor.IsAvailable()}}): {{NewestInstaller}} = installers whose Name contains "scurebox" (ci) or file name starts with "scurebox" (ci), highest {{System.Version.TryParse(Version)}} (unparsable = 0.0), then version string ordinal desc. None → 9087 "No sCureBox package found on USB". Manifest = installer version + SHA-256 of its path. RunUpdate steps: {{find_usb}} ok → {{find_package}} (9087 NoPackageMessage) → if {{GetApplication().Version == installer.Version}} fail {{install_post}} "Version <v> is already installed" (9086) → {{verify_signature}}: {{Install(path)}} refused → "The supervisor refused the package: <reason>" (9086) → {{install_post}}: poll {{GetApplication}} every {{SupervisorPoll}} while it is null or {{State == "Installing"}} (ci) up to {{SupervisorInstallTimeout}} → "The supervisor did not finish the installation in time"; {{InstallFailed}} → "Failed at 'Installing update': <error or 'the supervisor reported a failure'>"; resulting version ≠ installer → "The supervisor reports version <x> instead of <v>"; all 9086 with Version. Success "Updated to version <v>". Note (ops): supervisor install does not restart the app; the host restarts afterwards (Api/Deploy-Ops).
*Configuration:* key file locations above; {{SCURE_SUPERVISOR_URL}} (via PLAT-07).
*Acceptance criteria:*
* A package built with {{UpdatePackageBuilder}} + key pair verifies and installs (fake script runner records {{--pre}}, {{--post}}).
* Signed with another key, or a tampered payload → fails at {{verify_signature}} with 9086.
* Missing USB → 9081; USB without {{.scu}} → 9087; newest file wins including {{scure-update/}}.
* A failing {{--post}} triggers {{--rollback}}.
* Builder throws {{FileNotFoundException}} without {{manifest.json}} or {{install.sh}}.
* Supervisor: picks newest sCureBox installer ignoring others; refused / failed / wrong-version / already-installed cases fail with 9086; without a supervisor the {{.scu}} flow is used.
*Tests:* {{Platform/UpdateServiceTests}} (Package_builds_verifies_and_installs, Extracted_package_contains_the_tree_and_the_signature_verifies_directly, Package_signed_with_another_key_is_rejected, Tampered_payload_is_rejected, Missing_usb_and_missing_package_have_their_own_codes, Newest_package_wins_including_the_scure_update_folder, Failed_install_rolls_back, Builder_requires_manifest_and_install_script); {{Platform/SupervisorUpdateTests}} (The_newest_scurebox_package_is_chosen_and_other_installers_are_ignored, An_update_installs_the_package_through_the_supervisor, No_package_on_the_stick_is_reported_as_no_update_package, A_package_the_supervisor_refuses_fails_the_update_with_its_reason, A_failed_install_and_a_wrong_resulting_version_both_fail_the_update, The_version_that_is_already_installed_is_not_installed_again, The_application_reply_is_read_leniently, Without_a_supervisor_the_scu_flow_is_used) with a fake {{ISupervisorClient}} and tiny {{SupervisorPoll}}.
*Reference (source):* {{src/SCureBox.Application/Platform/{IUpdateService,UpdateService,UpdatePackage,UpdatePackageBuilder,IScriptRunner,BashScriptRunner,Update*Dto}.cs}}, {{deploy/keys/scure-update.pub}}

