*Behaviour & rules:*
# {{Status()}} Linux: ip = first {{inet}} {{local}} of {{ip -4 -j addr show eth0}}; if no eth0 at all (neither that nor {{ip link show eth0}}) use first address of {{hostname -I}}. {{carrier}}/{{address}} from {{/sys/class/net/eth0/}}; gateway = {{gateway}} of first entry of {{ip -j route show default}}; interfaces from {{ip -j addr show}} ({{ifname}}, UP when {{flags}} contains "UP", first inet). {{Connected = ip != "0.0.0.0" && (carrier missing || carrier == "1")}}. Off-Linux: {{NetworkInterface.GetAllNetworkInterfaces()}} excluding loopback; the first UP non-tunnel NIC with IPv4 gives ip/mac (lower-case hex with ':')/gateway. Exceptions (IO/Json/NetworkInformation/Access/InvalidOperation) → {{{Connected=false, Code=9084}}} + warning {{"[NET] status failed"}}. Finally {{Internet = internet() ?? Connected}}.
# {{WireguardIpOf}}: first interface with non-empty IP and Status "UP" whose lower-case name is {{wt<digits>}} or {{wg<digits>}} (length > 2), or contains "netbird" or "wireguard"; else "".
# {{Diagnostics(tool, address)}}: tool default "ping"; address default "8.8.8.8" (trimmed). Unknown tool → {{(false, "Unknown tool", 9080)}}; invalid address → {{(false, "Invalid address", 9085)}} — nothing is run. Commands (45 s timeout): Linux {{ping -c 4 -W 3 <a>}}, {{traceroute -m 15 -w 3 <a>}}, {{nslookup <a>}}; Windows {{ping -n 4 -w 3000}}, {{tracert -h 15 -w 3000}}. Exit -1 → {{(false, stderr, 9085)}}; otherwise {{(true, (stdout + "\n" + stderr).Trim())}} even on a non-zero exit (unreachable host output is the diagnostic).
# {{NetworkAddress.IsValidHostOrIp}}: null/blank or > 253 chars → false; valid IPv4 (regex {{^(25[0-5]|2[0-4]\d|1\d\d|[1-9]?\d)(\.(...)){3}$}} + {{IPAddress.TryParse}} InterNetwork) → true; IPv6 chars {{^[0-9A-Fa-f:.]{2,45}(%[A-Za-z0-9]{1,15})?$}} + parses as InterNetworkV6 → true; hostname RFC1123 {{^(?!-)[A-Za-z0-9-]{1,63}(?<!-)(\.(?!-)[A-Za-z0-9-]{1,63}(?<!-))*\.?$}} and NOT all-numeric {{^[0-9.]+\.?$}}. Rejects spaces, {{;}}, {{|}}, {{-c}} style options.
# {{PrefixLength(mask)}}: valid IPv4 whose bits are contiguous ones → popcount (255.255.255.0 → 24, 0.0.0.0 → 0); else null.
# {{SetStatic}}: off-Linux → Success "Network config simulated (off-device)". subnet default "255.255.255.0". Connection name = NAME of {{nmcli -t -f NAME,DEVICE connection show --active}} line whose device (after last ':') is {{eth0}}, else "eth0". DHCP: {{nmcli connection modify <c> ipv4.method auto ipv4.addresses "" ipv4.gateway "" ipv4.dns ""}}. Static: validate ip ("Invalid IP address '<ip>'"), gateway ("Invalid gateway '<g>'"), mask ("Invalid subnet mask '<m>'"), DNS list split on ',' or ' ' all IPv4 ("Invalid DNS '<d>'"), all code 9084; {{nmcli connection modify <c> ipv4.method manual ipv4.addresses <ip>/<prefix> ipv4.gateway <gw> [ipv4.dns a,b]}} (15 s). Then {{nmcli connection up <c>}} (30 s). Failures → Fail(stderr or "nmcli modify failed"/"nmcli up failed", 9084). Success "Network configuration applied".
# {{NetworkPolicy}}: file {{DataDir/network-policy.json}} = {{{"offline": true|false|null}}} (indented, atomic). {{ExpectsNetwork}} = operator choice when set ({{!offline}}), else {{cloudEnrolled()}}; if that throws → false (cannot tell = do not complain). {{Choose(null)}} returns to "follow cloud enrolment". Unreadable file → choice null. Save errors swallowed. {{/api/state}} exposes {{offlineMode}} (Api area).
*Configuration:* {{data/network-policy.json}}.
*Acceptance criteria:*
* {{Diagnostics("ping", "8.8.8.8; rm -rf /")}} → code 9085 without running anything; {{Diagnostics("curl", ...)}} → 9080.
* {{PrefixLength("255.255.255.0") == 24}}, {{PrefixLength("255.0.255.0") == null}}.
* Interfaces {{[eth0 UP 192.168.1.5, wt0 UP 100.106.37.62]}} → wireguardIp 100.106.37.62; a DOWN wt0 is ignored.
* Status internet = probe value when non-null, else equals {{connected}}.
* Policy: no cloud + no choice → OfflineMode; cloud enrolled → ExpectsNetwork; explicit choice wins and survives a new instance on the same data dir.
*Tests:* {{Platform/NetworkServiceTests}} (Wireguard_ip_is_the_up_netbird_or_wireguard_tunnel_address, Address_validation, Subnet_mask_to_prefix, Diagnostics_reject_injection_and_unknown_tools_without_running_anything, Status_reports_the_internet_probe_or_mirrors_the_lan_state, Static_config_is_simulated_off_device); {{Platform/NetworkPolicyTests}} (A_machine_without_a_cloud_account_is_offline_on_purpose, A_machine_enrolled_in_the_cloud_still_expects_a_network, The_operators_choice_wins_over_the_enrolment_and_survives_a_restart, A_cloud_check_that_throws_never_turns_into_a_network_complaint, The_strip_stays_green_offline_and_goes_blue_only_when_a_network_was_expected — the last one exercises Process {{StatusLedService}}).
