Files: {{data/cloud.json}} (CloudConfig, indented), {{data/cloud_reports.json}} (sorted string array of run ids already uploaded), {{data/cloud_deletes.json}} (sorted string array of run ids to delete on the portal).
*Behaviour & rules:*
# Security: the machine key is a shared secret stored in plain text in {{data/cloud.json}}; it is sent both as header {{X-Machine-Key}} and as body field {{machineKey}} (Apps Script cannot read headers). Outbound only; no command actuates hardware.
# Load at construction: no file → off; incomplete → error {{cloud.json needs "url" and "key"}}; parse error → {{bad cloud.json: <msg>}}. Complete → enabled, log {{"[CLOUD] sync agent ON -> <url>"}}.
# {{Configure}}: url or key blank → Fail("url and key required"). Else write cloud.json ({{name}} blank → "CureBox", {{interval ?? 10}}), enable, clear error; message "Cloud sync agent started" or "Cloud sync config updated" when already enabled.
# URL: base = {{Url.TrimEnd('/')}}; if it ends with {{/exec}} use as-is, else append {{/api/agent/sync}}. Request timeout 30 s.
# {{Snapshot()}} JSON: {{name}}, {{state{chamberTemp, doorClosed, isHeating, isCooling, uvOn, internetOk, counters (= Hours())}}} (state read failure → {{{}}}), {{programs}} (user materials), {{presets}} (built-in catalog, separate field so the portal never offers edit/delete), {{prints}} (first 20), {{cures}} (first 10 runs serialized *without* {{telemetry}}), {{alertLog[{code, message, raised, cleared}]}} (unix s), {{ackIds}} (command ids applied in the previous sync). {{SyncOnceAsync}} adds {{machineKey}}.
# {{SyncOnceAsync}}: not configured → false. Sample alerts, POST snapshot (JSON, {{JsonDefaults.Options}}), {{EnsureSuccessStatusCode}}; reply {{{"ok": false, "message"}}} (Apps Script always 200) → error. For each object in {{commands[]}}: apply; acked ids = applied ones and also failed ones (exceptions Json/InvalidOperation/IO/Argument are logged and acked to avoid loops); unknown types are NOT acked. On success: {{LastSyncOk = unix now}}, error null, ack list replaced. If reply {{acceptsReports == true}}: run DeleteReports then UploadNextReport (their errors only logged). Transport errors (HttpRequest/TaskCanceled/Json/IO/InvalidOperation) → {{Error = message}}, return false; cancellation of the host token rethrows {{OperationCanceledException}}.
# Commands: {{upsert_program}} (payload → {{Material}}; replace same id or append; {{ReplaceUserMaterials}}), {{delete_program}} ({{payload.id}}), {{delete_print}} ({{payload.id}}; empty id → acked no-op; cure runs/reports stay), {{send_print}}: material by name among user + presets; duration minutes = {{payload.duration}} (minutes, number or numeric string) ?? {{ProgramEstimator.EstimateProgramMinutes(prog.Steps)}} when the program has steps ?? 20; {{PrintLog{ Id="cloud-<unix ms>", PrintName=payload.printName or "Job", MaterialName, PrinterName=payload.printerName or "CLOUD", Date=local "yyyy-MM-ddTHH:mm:ss", Duration=floor(minutes*60) seconds, Status="completed", Steps=program step count when >0 else payload.steps else 0, CsvFile=payload.csvFile or "", NfcTag=NfcUid.Display(payload.nfcTag) (malformed → null) }}} inserted first.
# Alert log ({{SampleAlerts}}, called every 1 s between syncs and before each sync): for each distinct code in {{state.Alerts}} open an entry {{{code, message = AlertDetails["<code>"] ?? "", raised = now}}} (an open entry's message is refreshed when a non-empty detail arrives); codes no longer present get {{cleared = now}}. Closed entries older than 48 h dropped; list capped at 300 (oldest removed).
# Report upload (one per sync): first run among the newest 10 with status ≠ "running" not in cloud_reports.json. Content = stored report when {{Format == "html"}} and non-empty; else build with {{ICureReportBuilder}} when the run has telemetry (context: material name, steps of the matching program by name, phase timings for the run id). Neither → mark done forever. POST {{{machineKey, kind:"report", runId, fileName (default "cure-report-<id>.html" or the builder's), materialName, startedAt, status, content}}} (60 s timeout); reply must be {{ok: true}}; then mark done.
# Deletions: {{CureHistoryDeletion.Delete/DeleteAll}} delete from the run store and {{Enqueue}} the ids. On a sync with {{acceptsReports}}, POST {{{machineKey, kind:"delete_reports", runIds:[...]}}}; on {{ok: true}} → {{Done(ids)}} and remove them from cloud_reports.json.
# {{ExecuteAsync}} loop: if enabled {{SyncOnceAsync}}; interval = {{max(3, enabled ? cfg.Interval ?? 10 : 3)}} s, waited in 1 s steps (via {{TimeProvider}}) calling {{SampleAlerts}} each second. Stops on cancellation.
*Configuration:* {{data/cloud.json}} {{{url, key, name="CureBox", interval=10}}}.
*Acceptance criteria:*
* Unconfigured: {{Status().Enabled == false}}; {{Configure(null, "k", ..)}} fails "url and key required".
* A sync posts to {{<url>/api/agent/sync}} with header {{X-Machine-Key}} and body {{machineKey}}; {{.../exec}} URL is posted as-is.
* Commands applied in sync N are listed in {{ackIds}} of sync N+1.
* HTTP 500 or {{{ok:false}}} sets {{Status().Error}}.
* A portal with {{acceptsReports:true}} receives each finished run's report exactly once; a deleted run's id is sent in {{delete_reports}} once; without {{acceptsReports}} nothing is uploaded.
* {{send_print}} for a catalog program uses its steps for steps/duration; a malformed {{nfcTag}} is dropped; {{delete_print}} removes the print.
* An alert raised and cleared between syncs appears in {{alertLog}} with both times.
*Tests:* {{Platform/CloudSyncAgentTests}} (FakePortal {{HttpMessageHandler}}, Harness): The_snapshot_carries_the_catalog_and_a_print_for_a_catalog_program_uses_its_steps, A_print_can_be_deleted_from_the_portal, A_malformed_nfc_tag_is_dropped, Unconfigured_agent_is_off_and_configure_requires_url_and_key, Sync_posts_the_snapshot_applies_commands_and_acks_them_next_time, Portal_errors_are_reported_in_the_status, An_ok_false_reply_is_an_error_even_with_status_200, A_google_apps_script_portal_is_posted_at_its_exec_url, A_portal_that_takes_reports_gets_each_finished_run_report_once, A_run_deleted_on_the_machine_is_deleted_on_the_portal_once, A_portal_that_does_not_take_reports_gets_none, Alerts_raised_between_syncs_are_logged_with_their_times, Incomplete_config_file_reports_an_error_and_stays_off.
*Reference (source):* {{src/SCureBox.Application/Platform/{CloudConfig,ICloudSync,CloudSyncAgent,CloudReportDeletions,MachineStateSource}.cs}}, {{src/SCureBox.Application/Contracts/MachineState.cs}} ({{CloudSyncDto}}), portal side {{cloud/google/Code.gs}} (in sCure-A, Kiosk-Web/cloud area)

