*Behaviour & rules:*
# File {{data/component_counters.json}} = {{{"led405": s, "led450": s, "coolingFan": s, "heater": s, "heaterFan": s}}} (seconds, rounded to 1 decimal on write). Load: missing keys 0, negatives clamped to 0; load error → warning {{"[COUNTERS] load failed (...) - starting from zero"}}.
# {{Sample(s)}}: {{led405 = UvOn && UvWavelength == 405}}; {{led450 = UvOn && UvWavelength == 450}}; {{heater = HeaterOut ?? (HeaterPwm > 0 when HeaterPwm not null) ?? IsHeating}}; {{heaterFan = FanRpmEach["FAN_HEATER"] > 0 || Fans["chamber_heating"] > 0}}; {{coolingFan = FanRpmEach["FAN_COOLING"] > 0 || Fans["chamber_intake"] > 0}}.
# {{Tick()}}: state read throws (InvalidOperation/NullReference) → skip; add 2.0 s to each ON component, mark dirty.
# {{RunAsync}}: {{PeriodicTimer(2 s, TimeProvider)}}; after each tick, if dirty and ≥ 60 s since last flush → flush. On cancellation exit and flush once more. {{Dispose()}} flushes. Flush IO errors → warning.
# {{Hours()}} = seconds / 3600 rounded to 1 decimal.
*Configuration:* none.
*Acceptance criteria:*
* With a FakeTimeProvider and UV 405 on: after 60 s advanced, file exists with led405 = 60; heater off stays 0.
* Reload from file; {{Hours()}} of 5400 s = 1.5.
* Heater fallbacks: HeaterOut wins; else PWM > 0; else IsHeating.
* A throwing state source does not advance counters.
