*Behaviour & rules:*
# LED calibration file {{data/led_calibration.json}} = {{{"back":f,"door":f,"left":f,"right":f}}} (indented). Load: defaults 1.0; each saved value clamped to [0, 1.5]; error → warning {{"[LED-CAL] load failed (...) - all factors 1.0"}}. {{Validate}}: null → "factors object required"; missing zone → "'<zone>' missing"; NaN or outside → "<zone> factor <v> outside 0-1.5"; else null. {{Save}}: validate (throw ArgumentException with the reason), round each to 4 decimals, write atomically, activate, log {{"[LED-CAL] saved factors: back=1.00, ..."}}. {{Reset}} = Save(all 1.0). {{ScaledOutputs(p, f?)}} = per zone {{round(clamp(p × factor(default 1.0), 0, 100), 2)}}. Physical output = clamp(requested × factor, 0..100).
# BOFA file {{data/bofa.json}} = {{{"connected": bool, "dutyPercent": int}}} (indented, atomic). Defaults: not connected, 10 %. Load clamps duty to 0..100; unreadable → not connected, 10 %. {{Choose(connected?, duty?)}} updates given fields (duty clamped 0..100) and saves (errors swallowed). Semantics (enforced in Process): only when Connected is the extractor ever driven; it runs whenever the air-intake fan runs; duty is a 0–10 V speed reference (PCA9685 ch 10, ×3.3 amplifier, ~0–10.9 V; scale not measured on a unit).
# SerialBackup: directory = ctor arg ?? env {{SCURE_SD_DIR}} (trimmed) ?? {{/mnt/ssd2/scure}}; file {{config_backup.json}} {{{serialNumber, deviceName, savedAt}}} (indented). {{Available}} = directory exists OR its parent exists (never create {{/mnt/ssd2}} itself — that would put the "backup" on the system disk). {{Read(out problem)}}: no file → null, problem null; empty serial → null + problem "the backup on the card (<path>) has no serial number in it"; parse error → null + "...could not be read: <msg>" (caller raises Err 3001). {{Write}}: blank serial → Failed(4003, "no serial number to back up"); not Available → Failed(4003, "no card mounted at <dir>: the serial number has no second copy"); else create dir, write {{<path>.tmp}} then move over (savedAt = UTC "O"); exception → Failed(4003, "could not write <path>: <msg>"). Note: Origin images have no removable medium and read-only root, so 4003 is raised on every Origin unit (known).
*Configuration:* env {{SCURE_SD_DIR}}; files above.
*Acceptance criteria:*
* LED: defaults all 1.0; {{{back:1.6,...}}} rejected; save persists and reloads; corrupt file → 1.0; out-of-range file values clamped.
* BOFA: fresh → Connected false, duty 10; {{Choose(true, 150)}} → duty 100 and survives a new instance; unreadable file → not connected.
* Serial: written serial reads back; writing again replaces; with no card (parent missing) Read → null and Write → code 4003; damaged file → problem text non-null; empty serial never written; default path is {{/mnt/ssd2/scure/config_backup.json}} and an unmounted dir is not created.
*Tests:* {{Platform/LedCalibrationStoreTests}} (Defaults_are_all_one, Validate_rejects_out_of_range_and_missing_zones, Save_persists_atomically_and_reset_restores_defaults, Corrupt_or_out_of_range_file_is_clamped_or_defaulted); {{Platform/BofaPolicyTests}} (first three tests are store-level; the remainder — extractor follows the intake fan, 24 V only while extracting, Err 9048 switch/connector contradiction — exercise Application-Process {{CureController}}); {{Platform/SerialBackupTests}} (6 tests listed above).
